Given the code below, what is the output?

num = 3
if num % 2 == 0:
    print('Even')
else:
    print('Odd')

What will be the output of the following code?

x = 10
if x == 10:
    print('Ten')
else:
    print('Not Ten')

What will be the result of the following code?

score = 85
if score >= 90:
    print('A')
elif score >= 80:
    print('B')
else:
    print('C')

Consider the code below. What is the output?

num = 15
if num % 3 == 0 and num % 5 == 0:
    print('FizzBuzz')
elif num % 3 == 0:
    print('Fizz')
elif num % 5 == 0:
    print('Buzz')
else:
    print(num)

